+ * The header is not part of the signed bytes, but every field in it is bound:
+ * `kind` selects the domain-separation context, `suite` must match the key's
+ * algorithm, `kid` is recomputed from `pk`, and `pk` is the key the signature
+ * must verify under. Swapping any of them makes verification fail or surfaces
+ * an unknown issuer.
